      "text": "N's pose binding is `ap/8865619b/k/8957d119.json` (SHA256 `8957d119bfa6776efe776816675da6d0f610a6e8c336acd66c297f29cf4e7e0f`). It is a `c1-pose-mix-v1` spec over raw a2v3 (database `b32359ce256a567912d6436fac95dcab78bcef3bb2e1154cabdca57bacdc5320`, receipt `30612832`, frame prefix `/data2/k7pd/`), then raw a3v2 (database `0b95850a2dec57ec6702ca72cd198eb5afdcdcdd5f711a76a878104e30ec3571`, receipt `1e7b491b`).\nN's configs (build 20 `5257a297`, n1fix2 `8063ef04`, build 21 `8c610a6e`) bind BENCH v2 (`3119aa4a9594e4507372b99243afc8210fe217393466ac4e5ae78485e7c83970`) and dev (`a1869ae28f6d3f1815993da776f4c4798f67bad4c555c3bb80cc48fcecb23af5`). Sealed tree `780ca7b4` therefore applies both lists to every pose source in `carrier_c1_run.prepare` (`s1_exclusions.apply`), and `prepared()` re-derives that selection before training.\nRaw a2v3 holds 23 rows on venue 381879: 12 on `d3/41159526` (token `d3/vc6a4b809b958`) and 11 on `d3/41159521` (token `d3/vf3e2ed14c783`). Raw a3v2 and the venue's other captures hold none.\nEach of the 23 matches a BENCH v2 rung-1 token (VSI-Bench and ReVSI, room `arkitscenes/venue381879`) and no dev entry, so N's final scene filter rejects all 23. Two independent recomputations agree on every qid and on the full-source census.\nThe 23 also fail N's earlier dense/frame-prefix selection (`c1_pose_mix._row_selected`). Step 544 ran byte-identical selection code on the same spec and database, dropped no a2v3 row on exclusions, and its pre-filter order omits all 23.\nThe scene projections used here reproduce step 544's receipt census hashes on its indices for both sources, which binds them to the raw databases. No raw pose row on the 146 frame-pool captures or their room siblings escapes BENCH v2.\nN's exact admitted pose order and its SHA256 are **MISSING**. N has not prepared, and its configs cannot prepare until `r2_scene_rebuild` and `r2_sampling` are bound. That order will be the reader-filtered pose order that `r1_population.bind_prepared` writes, a checked subsequence of `pose_scene_order.json`.\nA replay also needs the full raw databases. They are absent on Trinity; verified copies are attested on Mind (`/lab_data/tarrlab/jacoby/agent_project/aws_evac/d/w19/evid/f02f16ad_s_a2v3_rows.sqlite`, `/lab_data/tarrlab/jacoby/agent_project/aws_evac/d/w19/pose/a2/ap_f02f16ad_s_a3v2_rows.sqlite`) and on GCS (`q9/8865619b/ca8d40ab9b55.p00-02`, `q9/8865619b/57ef13741a40.p00-09`).\nThis paragraph proves the 23 are excluded from N's pose family; the complete `data_rows_r2` record stays MISSING.\nReproduce with `OMP_NUM_THREADS=8 nice -n 10 /scratch/jjyeung/uv-python/cpython-3.12.13-linux-x86_64-gnu/bin/python3 -B work/prove.py` in `sb_posefam` and the same interpreter on `notes/pfrev.py` in `sb_pfrev`.\n"
    },
